Part of #20257. See plan §4 in the op-geth decoupling doc (PR #19767).

## Goal

Create `op-core/fees` containing OP-Stack L1 cost + operator-fee calculations. Consumers import as `opfees`. Sibling to `op-core/types` — no cycle (pure math on bytes + big.Int).

## Scope

Copy / port from op-geth's `core/types/rollup_cost.go` (Fjord-era subset only — earlier-fork cost funcs are unused in the monorepo):

```go
package fees

type RollupCostData struct { Zeroes, Ones, FastLzSize uint64 }

func NewRollupCostData(data []byte) RollupCostData
func (r RollupCostData) EstimatedDASize() *big.Int
type L1CostFunc func(RollupCostData, blockTime uint64) *big.Int
func NewL1CostFuncFjord(l1BaseFee, l1BlobBaseFee, baseFeeScalar, blobFeeScalar *big.Int) L1CostFunc

// New helper: replaces inline operator-fee math duplicated across
// op-service/txinclude/txbudget.go and op-service/txinclude/isthmus_cost_oracle.go.
// Isthmus formula: (gasUsed * scalar / 1_000_000) + constant.
// TODO (to track separately): Jovian formula switches to multiply-by-100 path.
func OperatorCost(gasUsed, scalar, constant uint64) *big.Int

// Replaces (tx *types.Transaction).RollupCostData() op-geth method.
func TxRollupCostData(tx *types.Transaction) RollupCostData {
    return NewRollupCostData(tx.Data())
}
```

Dependencies: only `common`, `uint256`, `math/big`, stdlib. No import of `op-core/types`. No cycle possible.

## Dependencies

None. Can start immediately.

